{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea","id":1390555,"title":"Deadlands idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-21T08:18:59-07:00","id":1390555,"title":"Deadlands idea","content":"What if in Deadlands, instead of having the Reckoning started by a Native American shaman, it was actually started by William Clarke Quantrill? Quantrill in real life was a Confederate sympathizer who led a group of guerrilla who massacred the people of Lawrence, Kansas in 1863. What if the massacre was actually a mass human sacrifice and brought the Reckoners to Earth? This would be both more historically accurate and more culturally sensitive by making a racist mass murderer the villain instead of a fictional Native American character.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:41:18-07:00","id":1390578,"title":"","content":"Nah, because having a racist strawman doesn't make anything better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:03:23-07:00","id":1390585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1390578#post1390578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, because having a racist strawman doesn't make anything better</div> </div> </div> </div>if it\u2019s a real person whose racism is historically accurate, he\u2019s hardly a \u201cstraw man\u201d. That term implies a hyperbole created to be easier to argue against than the truth. So to the extent that Deadlands suffers from demonizing Native resistance to genocide, I do think reassigning responsibility there may be a good idea, at least for a lot of people\u2019s tables.<br /> <br /> i have considered pushing back the timeline and making the original unleashing be something the Klan did as an act of revenge for the defeat of the Confederacy and abolition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:09:37-07:00","id":1390588,"title":"","content":"Possibly talking a different edition here, but my two cents.<br /> <br /> So, how would Quantrill know about this, and what would his motivation have been? The Confederacy's standing in the war was an incidental thing that resulted from the appearance of ghost rock not a designed thing because the Reckoners and the Manitou don't care about sides in that conflict. So why would a racist suddenly decide &quot;Hmm you know I've got no proof of it, but maybe those ignorant savages actually have working magic that I can unleash to further the cause.&quot; The most likely option would be having it be done on accident, but at that point it doesn't matter that the person doing it was a bad person since at worst they're the unfortunate dupe of the Reckoners and their morality is irrelevant. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:38:11-07:00","id":1390594,"title":"","content":"Maybe don't focus solely on the man's race and instead look at his motivations. A man, driven by grief and dispar over the loss of his people turned to some dark powers for revenge. Hes not some mustache twirling plantation owner going &quot;Muh slaves!&quot; Whitewashing the setting completely invalides the native American factions trying to fight the darkness. It also turns everyone south of the Mason dixon into a cartoon villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 05-21-2020, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T11:51:27-07:00","id":1390597,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it takes a lot of the nuance out of the setting. Raven was always the most interesting antagonist, even going on to declare war on his former masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T12:36:32-07:00","id":1390602,"title":"","content":"A thing on my part, I admit I haven't read most of the modules and such for the Weird West setting but I don't recall Raven being portrayed as a major villain. Like maybe I'm missing something, but my knowledge till you got to Hell on Earth he was more of a thing that existed to explain how the situation happened. If we were going with actual <i> human </i> villains beyond the Reckoners then Stone would probably fill that role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T12:42:36-07:00","id":1390604,"title":"","content":"Stone is their agent on earth, Raven hangs out in the spirit lands doing spirit land things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:00:58-07:00","id":1390606,"title":"","content":"Raven is central, but not in a &quot;lets go shoot the son of a bitch&quot; way. He has a massive network of agents, the cult of the raven, ties to both the Coyote Confederation and the Souix Nation. And y'know has a big metaplot role.<br /> <br /> My 7 year campaign had Raven as the big bad, ferreting out his cultists, repairing relations between the factions that he'd broken. This was years before Last Sons came out and all of my possie had serious respect for him as an enemy, mostly because he ahs actual plans they can interfere with. Stone just wanders around shootin folks, Gimme is sat in LA as it's ruler, and Helstromme is likewise mostly in his lab. Chasing Ravenites took them all over the continent, coast to coast, from Canada to Mexico...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:25:27-07:00","id":1390612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1390594#post1390594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe don't focus solely on the man's race and instead look at his motivations. A man, driven by grief and dispar over the loss of his people turned to some dark powers for revenge. Hes not some mustache twirling plantation owner going &quot;Muh slaves!&quot; Whitewashing the setting completely invalides the native American factions trying to fight the darkness. It also turns everyone south of the Mason dixon into a cartoon villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again - you\u2019re talking like portraying the evil of the eras slavers is some how hyperbolous. There is a point where prentending the founders of the KKK were nuanced people is disingenuous Grey washing of real human evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:36:17-07:00","id":1390615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1390612#post1390612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again - you\u2019re talking like portraying the evil of the eras slavers is some how hyperbolous. There is a point where prentending the founders of the KKK were nuanced people is disingenuous Grey washing of real human evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as disingenuous as says the actions of one fictional man who happens to be a native American somehow demonizes their entire struggle against genocide<br /> <br /> And simply saying the motivations of the Klan founders were &quot;ok we evil now&quot; shows a lack of knowledge on the subject.<br /> <br /> Before you start, no I'm not defending the Klan. What they did was monstrous and inhuman but to water down their motivations is a disservice to history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 05-21-2020, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:43:54-07:00","id":1390638,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. This discussion is really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:46:44-07:00","id":1390639,"title":"","content":"I figured maybe Quantrill was trying to open a doorway to Hell to bring in demons to destroy the Union army and got the Reckoners instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T15:57:16-07:00","id":1390643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1390639#post1390639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured maybe Quantrill was trying to open a doorway to Hell to bring in demons to destroy the Union army and got the Reckoners instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why then and not during the bleeding Kansas years of 1855 \u2013 1861?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T16:02:51-07:00","id":1390646,"title":"","content":"Because that\u2019s when Quantrill massacred the people of Lawrence. 1863. Him and Bloody Bill Anderson. This really happened.<br /> <br /> Quantrill\u2019s Raiders operated in Kansas throughout the Civil War until Quantrill was tried and hanged for treason and war crimes sometime in 1865.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T16:04:36-07:00","id":1390647,"title":"","content":"My grandfather told me about it. His father was a Pinkerton operative and he heard the story when he was stationed in the Lawrence for a couple months back in the Thirties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T16:11:45-07:00","id":1390649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1390646#post1390646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantrill\u2019s Raiders operated in Kansas throughout the Civil War until Quantrill was tried and hanged for treason and war crimes sometime in 1865.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was wounded in battle (paralyzed from the chest down) and died of his wounds in june 1865. But hey if we are spitballing angry guys with a grudge why not John Brown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T16:26:17-07:00","id":1390652,"title":"","content":"It just feels like it would taint the game personally speaking. I may have tipped my hand about how Raven is one of my favourite big bads, replacing him with Quandrill takes a lot of the shine off.<br /> <br /> Couldn't you just have Quandrill do his summoning thing after the Reconing? Would have even more of an irony, trying to summon the devil but unleashing something worse that he doesn't understand, because, surprise surprise, bloodthirsty nutcase thinks his mythology is right but it's oh so wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T17:31:16-07:00","id":1390663,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3953_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3953\" data-vbnamecard=\"3953\">Dwight</a> John Brown was cool. Cloudsplitter. God\u2019s Angry Man. He wouldn\u2019t get involved with the Reckoners.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1037_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1037\" data-vbnamecard=\"1037\">jamiemalk</a> good idea. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T17:49:26-07:00","id":1390668,"title":"","content":"Might i suggest a Wakin' Nightmare as what answered, those things are bad news. Haunting Quandrill everynight, killing anyone who trys to aid him after slaughtering all his men in front of him. Can have a possie find him as a broken shell of a man. Could change the weakness to only an karmic one, like only once Quandrill has gained forgiveness from a relative of one of the sacrificial victims can it finally be put down for good...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T18:20:52-07:00","id":1390672,"title":"","content":"Perfect<br /> <br /> Cool sig","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T21:26:01-07:00","id":1391626,"title":"","content":"I have, over the decades, toyed with various ideas of alternate variations and histories for Deadlands. (It's one of those games where I like in theory, but a number of its parts always bugged me to varying degrees. Things like the Civil War lasting for a generation, the South just up and deciding to end slavery - which always felt a little bit like a cop out - and so forth.) At some point, I mostly settled on the idea of moving the catalyst to 1862 and the Battle of Antietam (which was the single bloodiest day of the war). Rather than a single spell caster, I went with the idea of multiple ones around the globe, usually reflective of whatever region they were in. This included your evil Chinese wizard (who has probably been conducting mini rituals throughout the Taiping Rebellion, especially during and after the battle of Shanghai), your evil British druids and/or hellfire club type cult, your evil Egyptian mummy awakened during the early years of Egyptology, Dracula having been kept alive through the black magic of the Scholomance, the New Orleans voodoo bokur whose name I'm blanking on, some sort of Aztec sect in Mexico, a New England witches coven (one in the Hammer Horror film mold), a European mad scientist, and so on. And yes, this probably includes a Navajo skin walker and some other Native villains. So, this sort of weird horror adventure is a global phenomenon that reflects a lot of the tropes of those regions. <br /> The Civil War turns into a stalemate, and in 1864, George McClellan with the US Presidency as the Democratic candidate on a peace platform and the war is soon over. Lincoln goes back west, eventually turning into a 19th century version of Daredevil crossed with the Lone Ranger or the Shadow, being a crusading lawyer by day and masked vigilante (and monster hunter) by night. Meanwhile, in the South, a modern day Moses appears, gifted with divine power, and leads almost all the slaves to the new promise land in the West (probably the Cascades region or there about). The Southern economy pretty much collapses, and the British and French offer economic assistance only on the condition of ending what little slavery still exists. Texas eventually succeeds from the CSA, with the idea of establishing its own empire in the west at the expense of Mexico, various Native lands, and eventually California. (This proves harder than expected, even with the technological advances provided by strange artifacts found around Roswell. The Comanche and Apache are especially difficult to &quot;tame&quot;, as are Mexican freedom fighters originally organized by the late Benito Juarez. The dinosaurs are also an issue.) The CSA is still struggling, effectively starting to turn in a banana republic (or would that be cotton republic) under British and French business interests, and even efforts to gin up a war of conquest against Cube isn't really helping. A lot of Southerners have gone west. A lot of these were pro-Unionists who wanted to live in US territory, while others are soldiers who feel that they were used in a pointless cause, by landed gentry who have sold their states out to foreign interests. But most of them are just looking for work and a new start. The Union, meanwhile, has embraced industrialization, taking on this weird and at times grimy steampunk look and feel, complete with exploited immigrants and labor movements (as well as suffragettes) contrasted with a gilded age upper class. New Orleans is effectively an independent city state, largely run by its black and mixed race population (who strangely didn't follow the new Moses west).<br /> Out West are a number of Native nations, including the Sioux, the Comanche, the Apache, the Navajo, the Sequoyah Confederation (Oklahoma), and others. Actually US control runs from the Midwest through Kansas and most of Colorado before bumping into a now independent Mormon Deseret. After the Great Quake, Baja California and part of Southern California's coast have split off into a series of islands, sometimes referred to as the Great Maze. (This is entirely an excuse to have cowboys fight sea monsters.). San Fransisco and the Bay Area are still intact, and while damaged by the quake are mostly rebuilt, with a massive influx of Chinese and other immigrants. However, California is almost entirely independent as its own Republic, owing to how difficult it is to get help from back east. <br /> The British North American Act never passed and the Dominion of Canada doesn't exist. The Maritime areas are still their own thing, as is British Columbia. The Quebec part of the Provence of Canada is growing increasingly rebellious and independence minded, taking some cues from the successful Red River Rebellion that established a separate independent territory. The Cree, Blackfoot, and other First Nations also have their own lands. Alaska is still Russian. <br /> Mexico is still the Empire of Mexico under Maximillian, but has been in a constant state of civil war with nationalist republicans since its creation. Incursions by the Republic of Texas only complicate matters, as both sides are technically allied against the invaders, but in practice tend to constantly betray and undermine each other. The Yucatan is an independent region, largely under the control of its native peoples. <br /> Elsewhere, the Meiji Restoration continues with an increasingly steam tech feel to it. The Qing Dystasty has mostly reassured control over China after the rebellion, but at the expense of allowing further foreign concessions in exchange for aid. Both Britain and France are adapting ghost-rock steam tech, but no where near as quickly or as totally as Prussia. (Neither the Franco-Prussian War nor German unification has happened; Instead, Prussia is just becoming increasingly militant.)<br /> <br /> Also I call ghost rock &quot;Unobtainium&quot; or the like, just to give it a scientific name. It also comes in a liquid form, easily processed into lightweight new materials by companies like DuPont, which seems to be fairly common in places like Texas, Sequoyah, Mexico and parts of Pennsylvania. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T22:17:10-07:00","id":1391862,"title":"","content":"In the new edition they are tweaking the timeline a bit due to the &quot;Morgana Effect&quot; and the CSA will have lost the Battle of Washington and the North and the South will be reunited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T03:44:41-07:00","id":1391888,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar490_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"490\" data-vbnamecard=\"490\">omenseer</a> you mean Deadlands Reloaded?<br /> <br /> What\u2019s the Morgana Effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-nam