seer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T14:25:03-07:00","id":1392317,"title":"","content":"I love that book! I think he meant in an RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T21:06:21-07:00","id":1392411,"title":"","content":"She tends to get more balanced treatment in fiction than, say, RPGs or comic books. (I was honestly a little surprised she wasn't used in Disney's Gargoyles series, but given how heavily they were apparently trying to set up a King Arthur spin off near the end of season two, they were probably saving her for that.)<br /> <br /> Regarding Deadlands, in addition to the Huxsters magic, Voodoo, Native shamanism, divine blessing, kung fu, and ghost-rock mad science, I also liked to incorporate &quot;white magic&quot; style ritual witchcraft (drawing on various Hermetic, Celtic and Germanic sources), psychic spiritualism, Mexican bruja magic, Kabbalism, Satanic black magic, and Egyptian/Masonic stuff.<br /> <br /> But then I also liked to think of Hell on Earth as a totally different world that was the same up until the Cuban Missile Crisis turned into a nuclear exchange (with some hints that the development of atomic weapons included some sort of occult Reckoners related significance) for a Wasted West setting based entirely on 1950s sci fi, western, and teen delinquent movie tropes with bits of 50s TV references and nods to the weirder aspects of the 40s and 50s in what is effectively Buddy Holly and the Atomic Hotrod Outlaws of Doom on a journey to Lost Vegas, so I am weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T21:26:31-07:00","id":1392413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392411#post1392411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She tends to get more balanced treatment in fiction than, say, RPGs or comic books. (I was honestly a little surprised she wasn't used in Disney's Gargoyles series, but given how heavily they were apparently trying to set up a King Arthur spin off near the end of season two, they were probably saving her for that.)<br /> <br /> Regarding Deadlands, in addition to the Huxsters magic, Voodoo, Native shamanism, divine blessing, kung fu, and ghost-rock mad science, I also liked to incorporate &quot;white magic&quot; style ritual witchcraft (drawing on various Hermetic, Celtic and Germanic sources), psychic spiritualism, Mexican bruja magic, Kabbalism, Satanic black magic, and Egyptian/Masonic stuff.<br /> <br /> But then I also liked to think of Hell on Earth as a totally different world that was the same up until the Cuban Missile Crisis turned into a nuclear exchange (with some hints that the development of atomic weapons included some sort of occult Reckoners related significance) for a Wasted West setting based entirely on 1950s sci fi, western, and teen delinquent movie tropes with bits of 50s TV references and nods to the weirder aspects of the 40s and 50s in what is effectively Buddy Holly and the Atomic Hotrod Outlaws of Doom on a journey to Lost Vegas, so I am weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was Witchcraft introduced in Hell on Earth reloaded. It could be considered Not-Black at least as it is not powered by the Reckoner's unlike the general Black Magic arcane background. Which craft will be in the new edition's companion, so maybe they will include trapping options for the various types of witchy mojo? They do have psychics, but not the spiritual kind though.<br /> <br /> Kind of like Fallout, but without the power armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T21:42:16-07:00","id":1392415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392413#post1392413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like Fallout, but without the power armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallout, Six-String Samurai, Cadillacs &amp; Dinosaurs, Mad Max/The Road Warrior if all the cars were 50s and early 60s hot rods, Tales from the Crypt comics, that kind of thing. Plus a bunch of people whose entire idea of the Wild West is based entirely on 1940s and 50s cowboy movies, and think &quot;civilization&quot; is a mix of Leave it to Beaver and I Love Lucy combined with bits of Film Noir, Robert Heinlein's early young adult novels, and Golden Age of Hollywood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-29-2020, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T22:01:20-07:00","id":1392417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392415#post1392415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fallout, Six-String Samurai, Cadillacs &amp; Dinosaurs, Mad Max/The Road Warrior if all the cars were 50s and early 60s hot rods, Tales from the Crypt comics, that kind of thing. Plus a bunch of people whose entire idea of the Wild West is based entirely on 1940s and 50s cowboy movies, and think &quot;civilization&quot; is a mix of Leave it to Beaver and I Love Lucy combined with bits of Film Noir, Robert Heinlein's early young adult novels, and Golden Age of Hollywood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not too far off from a character a friend of mine played in The Worm Turns plot point campaign. He was a David Carradine type who's monastery only had movies and TV shows from the 60s and before. There were more than a few Gilligan's Island references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T01:29:50-07:00","id":1392445,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> Interesting! I like the Hell on Earth idea. Tbh I only read one Hell on Earth book and couldn\u2019t get a single idea out of it (unless you count thinking Leland Throckmorton sounds a lot like Donald Trump), but you interpretation makes it sound a lot more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:58:17-07:00","id":1392501,"title":"","content":"Man I really need to get into Deadlands!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:31:08-07:00","id":1392590,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> you should buy the new Weird West core book when it comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:49:25-07:00","id":1392599,"title":"","content":"So what is the most up to date Corebook called?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:14:23-07:00","id":1392602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392599#post1392599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what is the most up to date Corebook called?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're just calling it Deadlands. At the very least you should be able to find with Deadlands SWADE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:15:56-07:00","id":1392604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392074#post1392074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that invalides the Hell on earth and Outpost settings</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no. They just recently updated Lost Colony to SWADE and they have said that Hell on Earth still happens. Its just the opening salvo happens a little differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T15:49:54-07:00","id":1392689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1390555-deadlands-idea?p=1392501#post1392501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I really need to get into Deadlands!</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/let\u2019s-read-deadlands-the-weird-west-rpg.862813/\" target=\"_blank\">pretty good WIR thread about the original core book</a> on RPG.net, including discussion about some of the setting issues and changes to it coming in the latest edition. <br /> <br /> The kickstarter campaign for the newest version can be <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/545820095/deadlands-the-weird-west\" target=\"_blank\">found here</a>. <br /> <br /> If you can turn your part of your brain off and accept the fact that it's written by people whose knowledge of the period, especially the Civil War and Native Americans, comes entirely from Hollywood Westerns, then it's a decently fun game. (One of the reasons I've never been able to get in to it as much as a lot of its hardcore fanbase is that I'm an armchair history and anthropology nerd, and my obsessive-compulsive tendencies made it impossible for me to stop picking those issues apart.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:11:58-07:00","id":1392691,"title":"","content":"I have no time for that kind of thread, the first two posts from the OP, urgh, not going to read any further.<br /> <br /> Its my favourite game, been playin' or Marshallin' for going on 20 years now, and not one person I've played with have ever seen it as something less than an awesome time for everyone involved...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:03:20-07:00","id":1392744,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1037_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1037\" data-vbnamecard=\"1037\">jamiemalk</a> not sure what a whippersnapper is, but you are defo a curmudgeon \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never actually played Deadlands, but it looks pretty cool and I\u2019ll probably check out the new edition when it comes out on DTRPG (plus I\u2019m looking forward to Deadlands Dark Ages cause I love medieval stuff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T22:41:23-07:00","id":1392760,"title":"","content":"Deadlands is one of those &quot;this is the way the world breaks&quot; ideas that can work well in most historical eras. I was actually always a little disappointed that, aside from the seperate WW2 game they made, they never tried making other settings like medieval dark fantasy adventure Europe, colonial gothic American Revolution, or the like. I kinda want to try it with 800AD Europe, with Charlemagne, Byzantium, vikings, Magyars, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T06:28:01-07:00","id":1392792,"title":"","content":"They did WWII Deadlands? What\u2019s it called? Is it on DTRPG?<br /